{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 79bee2fb90328e2f25863499940132263113c4ae (tree 46774aa2f35d7263fc37128c0e466281e1b76f9e), the Security stack on published 02d93554: S7, S10, S11 and the CLI deadline lane. Each lane has its own conclusions below. The verdict binds the four implementation promises 1ec027ec (S7), 2cde9dc0 (S10), 4bf8d639 (S11) and b00f6dd3 (CLI deadline), and signs all 24 path artifacts.\n\n## Evidence\n- **Artifacts.** The 24 filed artifacts equal the 24 changed paths (`git diff --no-renames --name-only 02d93554 79bee2fb`): no path missing, none extra, none twice.\n- **Gate.** `gate.txt` (SHA-256 `3b5a2c8b…`) names head 0dae0106, tree a04f7a98, changed files 0, and ends \"gate passed\", exit 0, 1,407.74 s. Node 246, Counting 60, Plain 5,087 with one skipped, Native 1,255 with two skipped, crossings 0 lost, 5 stale, 0 unowned. The review head differs from 0dae0106 only in the three evidence notes (tree 46774aa2 against a04f7a98).\n- **Hashes.** All 60 distinct SHA-256 values in the three notes match files in the retained evidence directories.\n- **Failed runs.** The four failed gates and the separate Native diagnosis keep their own logs and hashes in the notes. The Native diagnosis was run on repaired source. None of the failures is relabelled as a pass.\n- **Checks.** The merge into origin/main (02d93554) is clean with tree 46774aa2. `git diff --check` is clean. `check-commit-messages` flags none of 11 commits. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. The added lines carry no other project's name and no `/Users/` path outside the retained evidence directory.\n- **Moved-scale.** The notes say 16 cases across nine owners, the unit I verified on the S6 correction.\n\n## Wake rate\nThe stack adds no alarm, retry or reschedule. The wake floor is unchanged, and requests per room per hour are unchanged. S10 removes one Agent row read from each expired control. S7 adds outbound GitHub subrequests: a cold Site read on GitHub makes one request per object (commit, each tree on the path, blob) in place of one closure fetch. These are Worker subrequests, not Durable Object requests. The 30 s identity cache removes the repeated identity lookup. The cost is a few subrequests per cold read on a deep path, far under the paid-plan subrequest cap.\n\n## S7 Site reads (promise 1ec027ec)\n- **Architecture.** GitHub Site reads one object at a time, with the shallow and filter capabilities, instead of fetching a commit's closure. Artifacts Site keeps closure reads, and the note says why from recorded observations only. The wire bound stays the smaller of the configured maximum and 16 MiB; the isolated allowance is 18 times that. `defaultSend` is one module-level function, so the identity cache can compare transports in production. An isolated-allowance refusal maps to the same page 413 as before.\n- **Security.** The identity cache is keyed by a digest of configuration, repository and credential, so no raw credential is stored. A configuration, credential, repository or transport change forces another lookup. Failures are not cached, and the cache holds 128 entries for 30 s with oldest-first eviction. A replaced repository can stay undetected for up to 30 s. The note says so, and the read itself still authenticates with the credential on every request. The token owner is unchanged: its witness proves a held key still serves with the admission table full.\n- **Simplification.** One cache, one transport flag, one error mapping. Nothing to remove.\n- **Witnesses.** A real Git fast-import with 4,098 commits through Git's HTTP backend. Full mode refuses at the 4,096-object bound (`what: \"pack objects\"`). Isolated mode reads the three selected objects. The room-lanes witness goes through the production Site handler. Three controls distinguish (closure mode, shallow mode, cache hit).\n\n## S10 hosted control expiry (promise 2cde9dc0)\n- **Architecture.** `expiredBeforeAgent` runs first in `grant`, `connectionControl` and `#control_` (bearer, retire). The deadline is checked again after authority reads, so a request that expires during the read still refuses. A request with a bad signature falls through to the ordinary path.\n- **Security.** A validly signed but expired control now returns the one 400 `notAfter` answer without selecting an Agent row. It cannot probe Agent existence, and it does not reserve an operation, so the replay fence is untouched. The note states the existing durable-row cost and leaves the budget policy unchanged. With an unsafe clock the early check is skipped and the ordinary 503 path applies.\n- **Simplification.** One helper reused four times.\n- **Witness.** `test.each` over all five operations counts the Agent-row reads: the expired case reads zero, and a current request still reaches the 404 with exactly one read. That is a red per route with a paired control. The controls log is retained.\n\n## S11 IPv6 admission (promise 4bf8d639)\n- **Architecture.** `admissionAddressKey` groups IPv6 by /48 and leaves IPv4 and mapped IPv4 alone. Only the creation table and the hosted control and cleanup windows use it. `found` and signed reads keep the /64 key. The address check still runs before the key allocation. The arithmetic checks: 8,192 / 31 gives at least 265 addresses for creation, and 4,096 / 121 gives at least 34 for each control purpose. The test sees 121 rows after 120 admitted calls.\n- **Security.** One /48 can no longer rotate /64s to open windows: 300 /64s admit 30 keys and hold 31 rows. Another /48 and IPv4 are unaffected, and unique-local and mapped addresses behave as the tests state (link-local has no test). The bounded overflow window is unchanged.\n- **Simplification.** One new function and three call sites, with no new table or eviction rule.\n\n## CLI deadline and witness lane (promise b00f6dd3)\n- **Architecture.** `0a09f66acd` is a separate commit before the Security source. It gives four CLI integration cases 30 s deadlines and keeps their commands and assertions. Its message records the eight measured times: all four cases now run in 3.2 to 4.5 s on the stack against 30 s.\n- **Security.** Test-only change.\n- **Simplification.** Observation below.\n\n## Non-blocking\n1. **Residual /48 reach (docs).** `docs/security/entry-points.md` dropped the old sentence that one /48 holds 65,536 /64s. The residual case is a sender holding 265 or more /48s, which one /32 provides 65,536 times over. That sender can still fill the creation table and send every new identity to the shared overflow window. The new text says \"at least 265 distinct … /48s\" and leaves the reader to infer it. One sentence would state the remaining case.\n2. **Shared /48 allowance.** Every subscriber behind one /48 now shares 30 creations an hour. That is tight for a carrier or hosting /48 that serves many users. The note names the trade. Watch creation refusals after deploy.\n3. **Redundant overlap repair.** The execFile/`allSettled` overlap in `application-new.test.ts` (commit 0dae0106) duplicates the spawn environment. After the 30 s deadline it saves nothing: the case runs in about 4.3 s. The gate passed on it, so I do not ask for a change here. A later cleanup can drop it.\n4. **Note wording.** The S7 note records that the Plain comparison ran \"on incoming power\". The project retired power as a factor, so the sentence adds no evidence.\n\n## Deployment\nThe scope Durable Object, the room Worker and the MCP hosted Agent all change. Rollback is safe: no schema or table change ships. Read the DO rate after the deploy.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fcf94ad2dcbf4d93fb73e2c99d82c3bd8f87d99a","binding":"assigned","head":"79bee2fb90328e2f25863499940132263113c4ae","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:328dd62626681dbd6030ac8fdffc23442ce0c8d7\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1ec027ec03e59db56f1fc9cc2d950298826be101\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2cde9dc011bb281be66b2ecadc61dd059bb2fe59\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4bf8d639f84a095bf4130cb9beac3667331709e8\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b00f6dd348ffd95d3d95c5771ce92a7cdb92f596\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:328dd62626681dbd6030ac8fdffc23442ce0c8d7","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}